# BYOK — copy this file to `api-keys.properties` (repo root) and fill in your key.
# The sandbox app reads it at build time and injects it into BuildConfig.
#
# Leaving it blank (or not creating the file at all) is fine: the sandbox then runs
# detection + OCR + text removal and **skips translation**. That is still enough to see
# the pipeline work — you get the erased page, the detected boxes, and the Japanese the
# OCR read. Only the "translate + typeset" half needs a key.
#
# Any OpenAI-compatible provider works in the engine (see docs/PROVIDERS.md); the sandbox
# is hardcoded to this one key for convenience. The reader app does it properly:
# per-provider keys, encrypted with Android Keystore, set in its settings screen.
#
# `api-keys.properties` is gitignored — never commit a real key.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
